    "title": "KHP bust nearly 800 drivers for speeding over Memorial Day weekend in Kansas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matthew Self ,\n6 hours ago\nTOPEKA ( KSNT ) – State troopers made multiple DUI arrests and issued hundreds of speeding tickets over the Memorial Day weekend this year.\nThe Kansas Highway Patrol (KHP) announced in a press release the results for its Memorial Day Weekend Holiday Activity Report . The KHP said the reporting period started at 6 p.m. on Friday, May 22 and ended at midnight on Monday, May 25.\nTroopers worked two deadly crashes over the holiday weekend in Osage and Washington counties. You can find additional arrest and citation statistics for 2026 below:\nDUI arrests – 16 Speed citations – 786 Speed warnings – 819 Safety belt citations – 112 Safety belt warnings – 14 Safety belt teen citations – nine Safety belt teen warnings – two Child restraint citations – 12 Motorist assists – 472 Woman dies after west Topeka house fire For more local news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news in northeast Kansas by downloading our mobile app and by signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track Weather app by clicking here .\nFollow Matthew Self on X (Twitter): https://twitter.com/MatthewLeoSelf\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSNT 27 News.\n16",
    "summary": "TOPEKA ( KSNT ) – State troopers made multiple DUI arrests and issued hundreds of speeding tickets over the Memorial Day weekend this year. The Kansas Highway Patrol (KHP) announced in a press release the results for its Memorial Day Weekend Holiday Activity Report . The KHP said the reporting period started at 6 p.m. on Friday, May 22 and ended at midnight on Monday, May 25. Troopers worked two deadly crashes over the holiday weekend in Osage and Washington counties. Follow Matthew Self on X (Twitter): https://twitter.com/MatthewLeoSelf Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
